/** @file
  T6050 / J714s (Apple M5 Pro) native Apple AIC v3 Core System Resource Table.

  This is the Project Mu representation of the versioned, pointer-free ABI in
  drivers/AppleAic/aic3_csrt.h (struct ntasi_aic3_csrt_v1).  It is the AIC v3
  analogue of T602XFamilyPkg/AcpiTables/CSRT.aslc (which carries the AIC2
  "APPL"/"NTAS" record for T6020/J414s), and is byte-for-byte identical to the
  fixture emitted by drivers/AppleAic/emit_aic3_csrt.c "T6050".

  Envelope (exactly the T602X AIC2 form, only the vendor payload differs):
    - ACPI CSRT header, OEM ID "NTASI ", OEM Table ID "T605AIC3".
    - One Resource Group: VendorID "APPL", SubvendorID "NTAS",
      DeviceID 0x0008, SubdeviceID 0x0001 (the same IDs the AIC2 record uses,
      so a HAL that already matches the Apple AIC group matches this one).
    - One Resource Descriptor: Type 1 (interrupt), Subtype 1 (controller),
      UID 0, followed by the 144-byte ntasi_aic3_csrt_v1 vendor payload.

  Vendor payload (drivers/AppleAic/aic3_platform.c ntasi_aic3_t6050_fixture):
    signature "AIC3", aic_version 3, chip_id 0x6050, board_id 0x0008,
    controller_base 0x280400000 size 0x1cc000, event_base 0x280440000
    size 0x4000, config_offset 0x10000, nr_irq 3104, max_irq 4096,
    nr_die 1, max_die 4, all four strides 0x4a00, 18 CPUs.

  The normal profile publishes physical AIC lines without an alias tail.
  J714_NVME adds one ALI2 entry: GSIV 1001 maps to physical ANS IRQ 2338,
  which falls in Windows' reserved 2048..3071 ACPI IRQ range. The existing
  native HAL translates enable/accept while retaining physical EVENT/EOI.
  GSIV 1001 fits the captured ACPI.sys input range 0..1023 and is unclaimed
  in the live ADT interrupt arrays. This adds no interrupt emulation.

  The bytes below were generated by drivers/AppleAic/emit_aic3_csrt.c and
  transcribed verbatim; the 216-byte table disassembles cleanly under
  `iasl -d` as a valid CSRT and its ACPI checksum (byte 9 = 0x83) sums the
  whole table to zero.  Keeping the complete table as bytes makes ABI drift
  mechanically detectable, matching the T602X AIC2 CSRT convention.

  SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
**/

#include <Base.h>
#include <IndustryStandard/Acpi.h>

